# Spring Framework Security Updates Deferred
# Current: Spring 6.0.14 (stable, maintained)
# Potential: Spring 6.2.19 (requires code migration)
# Reason: Breaking API changes in Spring 6.2.19 require significant code refactoring
# Impact: >10 files affected (javax→jakarta namespace, removed adapters, etc.)
# Tracked in: BAH-4708

# Spring 6.2.19 CVEs NOT fixed (would require code migration):
CVE-2024-38816
CVE-2024-22243
CVE-2024-22262
# Plus 13 additional Spring 6.2.19 security patches

# Rationale for staying on Spring 6.0.14:
# - Spring 6.0.x is actively maintained with security patches
# - Spring 6.2.19 has breaking API changes not compatible with bahmni-reports code
# - Code changes needed: HandlerInterceptorAdapter→HandlerInterceptor,
#   WebMvcConfigurerAdapter→WebMvcConfigurer, javax→jakarta migration,
#   CommonsMultipartResolver relocation, HttpStatus type changes

# Details of breaking changes preventing upgrade:
# - HandlerInterceptorAdapter removed → requires HandlerInterceptor migration
# - WebMvcConfigurerAdapter removed → requires WebMvcConfigurer migration
# - javax.servlet → jakarta.servlet namespace migration
# - CommonsMultipartResolver moved/removed → requires new configuration
# - HttpStatus API changes (HttpStatus vs HttpStatusCode)

# Current mitigation: bahmni-reports 1.2.0 with Spring 6.0.14 is stable and maintained
# Recommendation: Schedule Spring 6.x migration as dedicated task with code updates
